  <section id="lab-pins" aria-labelledby="lab-pins-title">
    <h2 id="lab-pins-title">What the Labs Pin</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="{{ '/lab-kafka-debezium/' | url }}">Kafka + Debezium lab</a> and the
      <a href="https://github.com/{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/compose.yaml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">repository sandbox</a>
      use older images than the table above. A unit test fails if these values stop matching the
      compose files. No automated job starts the labs, so this is what they are configured with,
      not a record of a test run.
    </p>
    <table class="version-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">Versions pinned by the lab compose files</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Component</th>
          <th scope="col">Pinned in the labs</th>
          <th scope="col">Image</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Confluent Platform (Apache Kafka)</th>
          <td><code>{{ toolVersions.tested.confluentPlatform }}</code> (Kafka {{ toolVersions.tested.apacheKafka }})</td>
          <td><code>confluentinc/cp-kafka:{{ toolVersions.tested.confluentPlatform }}</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Debezium and Kafka Connect</th>
          <td><code>{{ toolVersions.tested.debeziumConnect }}</code></td>
          <td><code>quay.io/debezium/connect:{{ toolVersions.tested.debeziumConnect }}</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">PostgreSQL (lab page)</th>
          <td><code>{{ toolVersions.tested.postgresMajor }}</code></td>
          <td><code>debezium/postgres:{{ toolVersions.tested.postgresMajor }}</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">PostgreSQL (repository sandbox and observability compose)</th>
          <td><code>{{ toolVersions.tested.examplePostgresMajor }}</code></td>
          <td><code>quay.io/debezium/example-postgres:{{ toolVersions.tested.debeziumConnect }}</code></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The labs pull the Debezium images from <code>quay.io/debezium</code> by their full release tag. The floating
      <code>2.7</code> tag exists only on Quay, not on Docker Hub, so <code>debezium/connect:2.7</code> does not pull; and
      the Docker Hub <code>debezium/connect</code> repository has no tag newer than <code>3.0.0.Final</code>. Debezium
      {{ toolVersions.tools.debezium.version }} images are on Quay as well, so moving the labs to a current Debezium
      means changing the tag, and checking the Quay repository for it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The two PostgreSQL rows differ: the lab page runs <code>debezium/postgres:{{ toolVersions.tested.postgresMajor }}</code>, while the
      <code>example-postgres</code> image used by the repository sandbox is built upstream <code>FROM quay.io/debezium/postgres:{{ toolVersions.tested.examplePostgresMajor }}</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Confluent Platform {{ toolVersions.tested.confluentPlatform }} is past standard support: Confluent&rsquo;s
      <a href="https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/installation/versions-interoperability.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">versions and interoperability page</a>
      lists standard support for the 7.7.x line as ending on July 26, 2026. The labs are a teaching sandbox, not a deployment recommendation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="support-policy" aria-labelledby="support-policy-title">
    <h2 id="support-policy-title">Support Policy</h2>
    <dl class="status-legend">
      <dt><span class="status-badge status-stable">stable</span></dt>
      <dd>
        Production-ready release with stable APIs and comprehensive documentation.
        This is the vendor&rsquo;s status for the latest release, not a statement about what our labs run.
      </dd>
      
      <dt><span class="status-badge status-saas">saas</span></dt>
      <dd>
        Software-as-a-Service platforms that auto-update. Guides reflect current production behavior
        as of the last update date.
      </dd>
      
      <dt><span class="status-badge status-deprecated">deprecated</span></dt>
      <dd>
        Older versions that still work but should be upgraded. Guides may reference newer patterns.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="compatibility" aria-labelledby="compatibility-title">
    <h2 id="compatibility-title">Compatibility Notes</h2>
    
    <h3>Debezium + Kafka</h3>
    <p>
      The labs pin Debezium {{ toolVersions.tested.debeziumConnect }} with Confluent Platform {{ toolVersions.tested.confluentPlatform }}
      (Kafka {{ toolVersions.tested.apacheKafka }}). For which Kafka Connect, Java and database versions a Debezium release was
      tested against, consult the tested-versions table on the
      <a href="https://debezium.io/releases/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Debezium releases page</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Kafka Connect</h3>
    <p>
      Kafka Connect is bundled with Apache Kafka, and its version numbers align: the latest, Kafka {{ toolVersions.tools.kafka.version }},
      includes Kafka Connect {{ toolVersions.tools.kafkaConnect.version }}. The Debezium Connect image
      carries its own Connect worker.
    </p>

    <h3>PostgreSQL (Source Database)</h3>
    <p>
      The lab page runs PostgreSQL {{ toolVersions.tested.postgresMajor }} via the Debezium-tuned container image; the latest
      release is {{ toolVersions.tools.postgres.version }}.
      Logical replication is enabled out of the box so you can register the connector without extra Postgres configuration.
    </p>

    <h3>Cloud Platforms</h3>
    <p>
      AWS DMS, Fivetran, and SaaS CDC platforms use their own versioning schemes and handle updates automatically.
      Our cloud labs (<a href="{{ '/cloud-labs/aws-dms/' | url }}">AWS DMS</a>, <a href="{{ '/cloud-labs/fivetran/' | url }}">Fivetran</a>, <a href="{{ '/cloud-labs/goldengate/' | url }}">GoldenGate</a>, <a href="{{ '/cloud-labs/matillion-cdc/' | url }}">Matillion</a> and <a href="{{ '/cloud-labs/snowflake-cdc/' | url }}">Snowflake</a>) reflect current production behavior as of {{ toolVersions.lastUpdated }}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="update-frequency" aria-labelledby="update-frequency-title">
    <h2 id="update-frequency-title">Update Frequency</h2>
    <p>
      This version matrix is reviewed and updated quarterly by our automated site-content-review agent (<a href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}#freshness">Methodology</a> explains the freshness signals).
      If you notice a version is outdated, please 
      <a href="{{ '/errata/' | url }}">report an issue</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Next scheduled review:</strong> Check back after the start of each quarter (January, April, July, October).
    </p>
